From cfb650216d4fd78818a90b2d555e11a26822804e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MatroskaEditions: what playing an edition of a Matroska file
 means

A pure header that reads the editions the matroska demuxer exports
(ffmpeg-9940, the read-only "editions" option) and, for each, says
whether Kodi can play it and how: an edition that is not ordered plays
the whole file; an ordered one whose enabled chapters are parts of this
same file, ascending and without overlap, plays as the whole file with
the parts in between cut out (edit list cuts, a seek each), with gaps
and overlaps under 100 ms taken as parts that follow each other. A
hidden edition, or an ordered one that links other files, plays parts
out of order or twice, has a part without a start or an end, lies past
the end, or comes from a file of unknown length, is not offered, and
the reason is given.

Nothing calls it yet: the setting, the question when a file has several
editions and the cuts in VideoPlayer come in their own commit. It has a
host test (the exports of generated files read by the patched demuxer,
and synthetic cases) that eleven mutations make fail.
---
 .../DVDDemuxers/MatroskaEditions.h            | 282 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 282 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/MatroskaEditions.h

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/MatroskaEditions.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/MatroskaEditions.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..40beb88
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/MatroskaEditions.h
@@ -0,0 +1,282 @@
